From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] dcomp: the setters' overloads in MSVC's vtable order (animation first)

The dcomp transform, clip and effect interfaces overload their setters in
C++ (SetOffsetX(float) and SetOffsetX(IDCompositionAnimation *), ...). MSVC
lays out an overload set in reverse order of declaration, so the animation
overload comes first in the vtable. IDCompositionVisual already had it so;
the translate, scale, rotate, skew, matrix and 3D transforms, the rectangle
clip and the effect group had the value overload first. A caller built with
MSVC setting a value reached the animation setter with a garbage pointer:
the WebView2 runtime's scale transform for Office's Copilot pane.
---
diff --git a/dlls/dcomp/objects.c b/dlls/dcomp/objects.c
index d2ad010..4f80fd5 100644
--- a/dlls/dcomp/objects.c
+++ b/dlls/dcomp/objects.c
@@ -588,8 +588,13 @@ TRANSFORM_PROP(translate, IDCompositionTranslateTransform, OffsetY, 1)
 static const IDCompositionTranslateTransformVtbl translate_vtbl =
 {
     translate_QueryInterface, translate_AddRef, translate_Release,
-    translate_SetOffsetX, translate_SetOffsetXAnimation,
-    translate_SetOffsetY, translate_SetOffsetYAnimation,
+    /* As MSVC lays out the C++ overloads: the animation overload first (dcomp.idl). */
+#ifdef SG_MUTANT_DC_OVERLOAD_ORDER
+    (void *)translate_SetOffsetX, (void *)translate_SetOffsetXAnimation,
+#else
+    translate_SetOffsetXAnimation, translate_SetOffsetX,
+#endif
+    translate_SetOffsetYAnimation, translate_SetOffsetY,
 };
 
